From: rosy-port <ace@localhost>
Date: Sat, 22 Nov 2026 00:00:00 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] 1008 rosy: present 1125x2250 so the panel aspect is exact

UIKit renders the iPhone X canvas 1125x2436 (19.5:9, aspect 0.462) and the
kernel scaled it into rosy's 720x1440 panel (18:9, 0.500), which squeezed
everything ~8% vertically -- visible as a compressed lock screen.  Presenting
1125x2250 (375x750 points @3x) keeps the point width and @3x and makes the
copy uniform.  The ADT canvas-height in tools/rosy_facts.py is changed to
match.

---
 iokit/Kernel/arm/SweetFramebuffer.cpp | 12 +++++++++++-
 1 file changed, 11 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

--- a/iokit/Kernel/arm/SweetFramebuffer.cpp
+++ b/iokit/Kernel/arm/SweetFramebuffer.cpp
@@ -145,7 +145,17 @@
  * Boot-arg sweetfb_native=1 presents the real panel size instead.
  */
 #define SWEET_FB_LOGICAL_W              1125
+#if defined(ROSY)
+/*
+ * rosy's panel is 720x1440 = 18:9 (aspect 0.500), while the iPhone X canvas is
+ * 1125x2436 = 19.5:9 (0.462).  Scaling the latter into the former squeezes
+ * everything ~8% vertically.  1125x2250 keeps @3x (375x750 points) and matches
+ * the panel aspect exactly, so the copy is uniform.
+ */
+#define SWEET_FB_LOGICAL_H              2250
+#else
 #define SWEET_FB_LOGICAL_H              2436
+#endif
 #define SWEET_FB_FORMAT_BGRA            0x42475241
 
 /* defined below with the swap helpers; vinceZeroPresent() needs it earlier */
